    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0558" n="1392" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/143</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-23T16:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1920. Your 924, January 19, 12 a.m. I gave assurances as you authorized and have
                    received a written reply dated January 22 as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Netherlands Government hereby guarantee that the steamship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nieuw Amsterdam</hi> will immediately return
                            after her next homeward voyage. Signed, The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs, Loudon.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
